        fullContent: 'Neville\'s most radical claim is also his most essential: consciousness is the one and only reality. This is not a metaphor or a philosophical abstraction. He means it literally — the world you see, touch, hear, and experience is a projection of consciousness. The appearance of an external, independent physical world is an illusion. What appears "out there" is actually consciousness crystallized into form.\n\nThe ancient Hermetic principle "as within, so without" captures this perfectly, but Neville goes further by providing the mechanism. The conscious mind (which he personifies as the male principle) generates ideas and desires. The subconscious mind (the female principle) receives these ideas and gives them form and expression in the world. The subconscious never originates — it only accepts and expresses whatever the conscious mind impresses upon it through feeling.\n\nThis means that every condition in your life — your income, your relationships, your health — is an out-picturing of your inner state of consciousness. To change the outer, you must first change the inner. The world is a mirror reflecting your state of being, and no amount of manipulating the mirror will change the face it reflects. You must change your face — your consciousness — first.',
