        fullContent: 'Neville provides a precise, repeatable technique for manifesting any desire. The mechanism has three essential steps, and each must be performed correctly for the process to work. This is not wishful thinking or positive affirmation — it is a disciplined practice of consciousness.\n\nStep one: Define your desire clearly. Vague desires produce vague results. You must know exactly what you want before you can assume its fulfillment. Be specific — not in terms of "how" it will happen (that is not your concern), but in terms of the end result. What would your life look like if your wish were already fulfilled?\n\nStep two: Construct a short imaginary event — a scene — that implies your wish is already fulfilled. This scene should be brief (just a few seconds), sensory, and in the first person. For example, if your desire is a new home, you might imagine shaking someone\'s hand in congratulations as they hand you the keys. The scene must imply that the desire is ALREADY accomplished, not that it is in the process of happening.\n\nStep three: Enter a State Akin To Sleep (SATS). This is the drowsy, relaxed state just before sleep when the conscious mind is quiet and the subconscious is receptive. In this state, loop your imaginary scene over and over, feeling its reality with all your senses. Feel the handshake, hear the congratulations, smell the new house. Continue until you fall asleep in the feeling of the wish fulfilled.\n\nThe key distinction Neville emphasizes: you must imagine FROM the scene, not OF the scene. Feeling yourself IN the scene (first person) versus watching yourself on a screen (third person) is "the difference between success and failure."',
