        fullContent: 'An assumption, in Neville\'s teaching, is far more than a guess or a supposition. It is the conscious act of accepting a state as real and true, regardless of what your physical senses tell you. When you assume a state, you are not pretending or engaging in make-believe — you are exercising the fundamental creative power of consciousness. An assumption is a decree of consciousness, and consciousness is the only reality.\n\nEvery person alive is constantly making assumptions, though most do so unconsciously. When you worry, you are assuming an undesirable outcome. When you expect the worst, you are assuming a negative state. These unconscious assumptions are creative just as surely as deliberate ones — the law of assumption does not discriminate between conscious and unconscious use. It operates with mathematical precision regardless of your awareness of it.\n\nThe revolutionary insight Neville brings is that you can CHOOSE your assumptions deliberately. You can assume the state of your wish fulfilled even when every physical sense contradicts it. The assumption does not need to be "true" by 3D standards — in fact, it usually is not. But if you persist in it, if you sustain the feeling of its reality, it will harden into fact. This is the law.\n\nAn assumption is not an affirmation repeated mechanically. It is a felt conviction, a state of being that you enter and inhabit. The difference between saying "I am wealthy" and assuming the state of wealth is the difference between reciting a line and living a reality.',
